        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(openai): preserve authored openai-completions through provider normalization",
        "body": "Closes #105035\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWith the openai plugin runtime active (any real install), an explicitly authored `api: \"openai-completions\"` on the openai provider was silently rewritten to `openai-responses`: `resolveAuthoredOpenAICompletionsRoute` asked `resolveModelRoutes` for permission, and route-eligibility gating (`subscription-only-model-on-platform`, from #104685's auth-availability alignment) vetoed the authored route, so `normalizeResolvedModel`/`normalizeTransport` fell through to the Responses default.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMaintainer decision on #105035: an explicitly authored `openai-completions` api is a user contract and must survive plugin normalization. Route auth-availability alignment continues to govern unauthored/default route selection (its core consumer, `src/plugins/provider-model-routes.ts` via the provider policy surface, is untouched); it just no longer overrides what the user explicitly wrote. Authored routes now resolve their base URL as model → provider → `OPENAI_BASE_URL`/default. Net −7 prod LOC.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSetting `api: \"openai-completions\"` on `models.json`/`config.models.providers.openai` (provider- or model-level) is honored in every environment. Authored `openai-responses`, unauthored defaults, and the Codex-hooks route are byte-identical in behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Probe (worktree with plugin runtime loadable): `discoverModels(...).find(\"openai\",\"gpt-5.5\")?.api` prints `openai-completions` after the fix (previously `openai-responses` in the #105035 investigation).\n- `extensions/openai/openai-provider.test.ts`: 56 tests pass, including new table coverage — authored Completions preserved independently of route eligibility, environment base-URL fallback, authored Responses non-regression.\n- `src/agents/agent-model-discovery.test.ts` (the #104685/#105050 contract) stays green.\n- Codex Responses-only contract cross-checked against sibling `../codex` source (`codex-rs/model-provider-info/src/lib.rs`, `core/src/client.rs`).\n- Structured autoreview: clean (\"patch is correct\"); an earlier accepted finding (`OPENAI_BASE_URL` fallback regression) was fixed in-branch with a test.\n- Known edge (deferred): a `models.json`-only authored api without any `config.models.providers.openai` entry still normalizes to Responses in one transport-hook path because the hook receives no authored-source provenance without the config object; fixing that needs a core provenance seam and is out of scope here.\n",
